<%# PREVIEW - where a student's cash came from, and what it cost. One partial for both halves of the
    product.

    It was a card on the student's own portfolio page and a hand-written table on the admin record page,
    and the two disagreed on the **numbers**: the admin copy rendered Attendance, Math and Rewards and
    then printed `total_earnings_cents`, which also includes reading. On the seeded student that is
    $650.00 of rows under a $1,150.00 total, with the missing $500.00 named nowhere. A figure and its own
    breakdown cannot be maintained in two files - the same reasoning as one button base, applied to money.

    Locals:
      summary  - an EarningsSummary
      title    - optional card heading, omitted where a section heading already names it
      subtitle - optional line under that heading
      class    - extra classes on the card

    dl/dt/dd rather than divs: it is a list of terms and their values. Figures are tabular-nums so they
    read down the column. %>
<% paid = summary.total_earnings_cents.positive? || summary.transaction_fees_cents.positive? %>

<%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
           locals: { title: local_assigns[:title], subtitle: local_assigns[:subtitle],
                     padded: !paid, class: local_assigns[:class] } do %>
  <% if paid %>
    <dl class="divide-y divide-slate-100 text-sm">
      <% [["Attendance", summary.attendance_earnings_cents],
          ["Reading", summary.reading_earnings_cents],
          ["Math", summary.math_earnings_cents],
          ["Rewards", summary.awards_cents]].each do |label, cents| %>
        <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-3">
          <dt class="text-slate-700"><%= label %></dt>
          <dd class="tabular-nums text-slate-900"><%= number_to_currency(cents / 100.0) %></dd>
        </div>
      <% end %>

      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 bg-slate-50 px-5 py-3">
        <dt class="font-semibold text-slate-900">Total earned</dt>
        <dd class="font-semibold tabular-nums text-slate-900">
          <%= number_to_currency(summary.total_earnings_cents / 100.0) %>
        </dd>
      </div>

      <%# A deduction, so it carries an explicit minus as well as the colour - the same convention the
          holdings table uses for a negative, and it keeps the meaning off colour alone. %>
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5 py-3">
        <dt class="text-slate-700">Transaction fees</dt>
        <dd class="tabular-nums text-red-700">
          -<%= number_to_currency(summary.transaction_fees_cents / 100.0) %>
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  <% else %>
    <%# Six rows of $0.00 with a red "-$0.00" among them state nothing, and the minus on a zero is a wart
        the fees row cannot avoid. A student who has not been paid yet needs to know what pays them. %>
    <p class="text-sm text-slate-600">
      Nothing earned yet. Earnings arrive when a grade book is finalized.
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
